{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5YExMtR8PNyrRB8rYd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `saveAll` in `store.js`, but I have not run the tests. The shell was denied in this session, so the change is verified only by reading the code.\n\n**The bug:** `items.forEach(async ...)` discards the promises from each async callback. `saveAll` then returned `items.length` immediately, before any `db.put` had finished. A failed write also became an unhandled rejection instead of rejecting `saveAll`.\n\n**The fix** (`store.js:3-6`):\n```js\nasync function saveAll(items, db) {\n  await Promise.all(items.map((item) => db.put(item.id, item)));\n  return items.length;\n}\n```\n\nNow `saveAll` waits for every write to settle before resolving, and rejects if any write fails, which matches the header comment. The writes still run in parallel.\n\n**Not done:**\n- I did not run `npm test` (`node --test`). Bash was denied, and I did not try to get around that.\n- I did not add a test for the failure case. A useful one would make `db.put` reject for one item and assert that `saveAll` rejects. Say if you want it added."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":653,"cache_read_input_tokens":24858,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":653},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a4a1034-79ef-4cc0-b8f6-24ca53247047","uuid":"8875406c-0c4d-4b43-aee8-55407d3260df","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:34:34.783Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5YEoBPWwxP8c9cKajP"}
